# Echoing Deeps' "except it's a Cave in addition to its other types" is part of its copy effect, so it becomes part of the
# copy's copiable values (CR 707.9b): a Vesuva that later enters as a copy of the Echoing Deeps copying an Island is an
# Island and a Cave too, not a plain Island. Each enters tapped, as it copies something.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Masked Meower
Island
Echoing Deeps
Vesuva
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Masked Meower.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Masked Meower.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Discard 1 card)
Bot1.Choose(Island)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Echoing Deeps.Play
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Graveyard.Island)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Subtypes = Cave; Island
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Vesuva.Play
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Subtypes = Cave; Island
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Subtypes = Cave; Island
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Tapped = true
Bot1.Graveyard = Masked Meower; Island
